ontrolled GPIO), not left floating.\", \"evidence\": [{\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(net (code \\\"136\\\") (name \\\"unconnected-(U1-EN-Pad2)\\\") (class \\\"Default\\\") (node (ref \\\"U1\\\") (pin \\\"2\\\") (pinfunction \\\"EN\\\") (pintype \\\"input+no_connect\\\")))\"}], \"impact\": \"The 24 V to 5 V buck enable state is undefined. Start-up may be unreliable, and noise on a floating enable can cause spurious enabling or disabling of the 5 V rail.\", \"confidence\": 0.3}], \"summary\": \"The netlist shows R5 wired as a pull-up from the main-pump MOSFET gate to +3V3 (where its ATO counterpart R12 is a pull-down), which would energise the 24 V pump at power-up. The TPS62933 EN pin is also left unconnected, which is a less certain issue.\"}",
